Subject: Nursery: no process-wide pause; per-shape pretenuring and a reconcile gate lifted while a site is pretenured

What this does
  - The 98%-survivor pause of qjs_y_refill (y_pause, y_win_*, y_gate_prev) is removed: the nursery is never switched off.
  - Each shape the nursery makes cells with gets a site record (JSShape.y_site indexes qjs_ysite, 32 bytes: pre, tick, made, surv, am, as). A young cell keeps its site index in the first word of its unused list link (arrays store 0). Promotions count into surv, allocations into made; at the end of every young collection each touched site accumulates its epoch counts and, over at least 256 cells, becomes pretenured at >=98% promoted and young again below 95%. A pretenured site makes old cells except one in 64, which stays young to keep measuring. Interpreter plain objects and the compiled construct fill (q2_fill_new) both test and count.
  - While any site is pretenured the reconcile gate (qjs_y_gate, held while a unit is linked) is lifted, so parked garbage is freed in small batches while it is in cache.
  - QJS_Y_STATS prints the sites; the layout carries off_shape_ysite.

Why we need it
  With the pause removed and nothing else, Octane splay fell (plain 8173 -> 6445, AOT 9381 -> 8664: SplayLatency) because every cell survived one trip and then died as an old object. Pretenuring splay's sites restores it (plain ~8700-8900, AOT ~9460-9780) while earleyboyer's site (30-90% promoted) stays young.

Soundness
  The site index is read only from cells made by the three nursery allocation sites, all of which store it. A site index of 0 (table full, arrays) is ignored. STRICT, the differential corpus and the kit cases are clean.

Failure modes
  The decision lags by one collection; a site that changes behaviour is re-evaluated at the next collection once 256 cells have accumulated.

